Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 01:07:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0/9] media: venus: add SM7150 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add Venus (IRIS1) video decode support for the Qualcomm SM7150, tested on a
Google Pixel 4a (sunfish) running a mainline kernel.

SM7150 pairs an IRIS1 core with a firmware-managed power-domain model that the
existing venus resource data does not cover, so the bulk of this series is
teaching venus about that variant rather than new functionality:

 - The IRIS1 firmware reports its version with a different string layout, so
   hfi_msgs never parsed a version out of it (patch 2).
 - On this platform the firmware, not the driver, owns the core power domains.
   pm_helpers gains a path for that (patch 3).
 - New resource data, compatible and DT binding (patches 1, 5), plus the DTS
   nodes to enable it (patches 6, 7).

Three fixes are not SM7150-specific and stand on their own:

 - venus: core: bound sys_error recovery retries (patch 4). A firmware that
   fails to come back turns into an unbounded recovery loop today.
 - venus: free session buffers on error-path teardown (patch 8). Leak on the
   error path of session setup.
 - venus: hfi_platform: honor codec blacklist on the platform codecs path
   (patch 9). The blacklist was consulted on one path but not the other, so a
   masked codec could still be selected. On sunfish this matters because MPEG2
   has to be masked.

Decode is verified working on sunfish for H.264, HEVC, VP8 and VP9, both warm
and from a cold boot, via v4l2 and GStreamer. Encode is not addressed here: it
needs CVP support that does not exist yet, and the encoder is left masked.

Danila Tikhonov's patch is carried unchanged from the sm7150-mainline tree.

Danila Tikhonov (1):
  arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150: add venus video codec node

